## New components

### TitleCover

Stands in for a cover image: the title and the author set on a colored block, so the detail page has a visual anchor without uploads.

- Closest existing: Avatar, Card. Why not: Avatar draws initials in a circle of at most 56 px, and Card is a surface for content; neither sets a title in a 2:3 block.
- Built from: Truncate, tokens.fontSize.heading, tokens.color.entity.
- Box: 160 wide, 240 tall, padding 4, gap 2.
- Parts: title (The title, up to four lines, then cut with an ellipsis.); author (The author on one line at the bottom.).
- Layout: A 160 by 240 block at every width. The title sits at the top and the author at the bottom, both 16 inside the edges and 8 apart at the least.
- Behavior: Static. It shows the title and the author it is given; it has no interaction and no other state.
- States: default. ARIA pattern: none. Keyboard: none.
- Used on: S06.
"
